GitHub Webhook: GitHub → AWX


Inventory Troubleshooting
Error: Could not match supplied host pattern, ignoring: windows

because:
hosts: windows
existed in the playbook but no AWX group called windows existed. 

Error	Cause	Resolution
k3s.yaml permission denied	Root-owned kubeconfig	chmod 644
Could not match supplied host pattern	Missing AWX group	Create windows group
YAML is not in object format	Invalid syntax	Use YAML key:value
dict object has no attribute state	Missing state field	Add state: present
Syntax Error while loading YAML	Jinja syntax in vars file	Use pure YAML


Project Sync vs Job Sync
Project Sync
↓
Downloads latest Git code
Job Template Run
↓
Executes playbook using downloaded code
GitHub Webhook Configuration
AWX Template
→ Enable Webhook
→ Generate URL + Secret

GitHub
→ Settings
→ Webhooks
→ Add Webhook

AWX
→ Template
→ Enable Webhook
→ GitHub

Copy:
- Webhook URL
- Secret

GitHub
→ Settings
→ Webhooks
→ Add Webhook

Payload URL = URL from AWX
Secret = Secret from AWX
Content Type = application/json

Events = Push
3. Scheduled Automation
Projects
→ Schedules
→ Every 2 Minutes

Templates
→ Schedules
→ Every 2 Minutes

Upgrade Procedure
•	helm repo update
•	helm upgrade awx-operator ...

Logging and Troubleshooting
•	kubectl get pods -n awx
•	kubectl logs deployment/awx-operator-controller-manager -n awx
•	kubectl describe pod awx-web-xxxxx -n awx
•	kubectl get events -n awx

Troubleshooting:
Error: 
awx-web-57964945b9-hkkt4 Error
awx-web-57964945b9-9k4d9 ContainerStatusUnknown
awx-task-58c667d496-vf9c8 Init:Error
awx-task-58c667d496-wtl2s Init:Error
Steps of troubleshooting:
First, get the exact error
kubectl describe pod awx-web-57964945b9-hkkt4 -n awx
kubectl logs awx-web-57964945b9-hkkt4 -n awx
First, get the exact error
If logs fail because the pod restarted:
kubectl logs awx-web-57964945b9-hkkt4 -n awx –previous
Also check the task pod:
kubectl describe pod awx-task-58c667d496-vf9c8 -n awx

Check Operator Logs
kubectl logs deployment/awx-operator-controller-manager -n awx
Look for:
•	ERROR
•	WARNING
•	reconcile
•	failed

Check if AWX Secret Exists
kubectl get secrets -n awx
If present:
kubectl get secret awx-admin-password \
-n awx \
-o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d
Most useful command:
•	kubectl get events -n awx --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp
•	kubectl describe pod awx-web-57964945b9-hkkt4 -n awx
•	kubectl describe pod awx-task-58c667d496-vf9c8 -n awx
•	kubectl logs deployment/awx-operator-controller-manager -n awx

Confirm Disk Usage
•	df -h
•	sudo du -sh /var/lib/rancher/k3s/*
Check Node Storage Status
•	kubectl describe node awx | grep -A10 "Allocated resources"
•	kubectl describe node awx | grep -i storage
Check disk usage
•	sudo df -h
•	lsblk
increase disk space
EC2
•	→ Volumes
•	→ Select Root Volume
•	→ Actions
•	→ Modify Volume
•	→ Size = 50 GB
•	→ Save

Then Expand Linux Filesystem

Check disk layout: lsblk
You will probably see:
nvme0n1
├─nvme0n1p1
├─nvme0n1p13
└─nvme0n1p15
Then run:
•	sudo growpart /dev/nvme0n1 1
•	sudo resize2fs /dev/nvme0n1p1
•	df -h

Then Restart the Failed Pods
sudo kubectl delete pod -n awx –all

The Operator will recreate them.
Monitor:
kubectl get pods -n awx -w
